---
import Navigation from "../components/Navigation.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const pageTitle = "Stroop Says";
---

<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <title>{pageTitle}</title>
</head>

<body>
    <Navigation />
    <div class="mx-auto w-7/8 md:w-2/3 space-y-2">
        <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold">
            {pageTitle}
        </h1>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
            <blockquote class="my-auto italic p-3 text-secondary text-2xl font-semibold">
                A handheld game that combines the Stroop
                effect with the toy "Simon". 
            </blockquote>
            <iframe class="col-span-2 rounded-box" loading="lazy"
                src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/MtIXWUcXbPA?si=f5GZQNBSkwrXwuYO&controls=1&autoplay=0&rel=0&modestbranding=1"
                title="YouTube video player"
                allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
                referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
        </div>
        <div class="divider"></div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">
            Project Details
        </h2>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 my-4">
            <img class="rounded-box" src="../src/assets/images/stroop.webp" />
            <div class="col-span-2 space-y-4">
               <p>The objective of Stroop Says is to press the
                button that corresponds with the color the word is written in,
                rather than the word itself.</p>
                <p>
                    "Stroop Says" has two modes: memory mode and speed mode. In
                    memory mode, players observe a pattern and copy it, increasing
                    the length on each successful round. In this mode, the memory of
                    the pattern quickly overcomes the difficulty of the mismatched
                    stimuli from the Stroop effect.
                </p>
                <p>
                    In speed mode, players press the button corresponding to the
                    color of the word before time runs out. In this mode, the effect
                    is in full force. The colors and words alternate between periods
                    of matching and non-matching. The rhythm illustrates how hard it
                    is to separate the stimuli when they are no longer matching, and
                    making it more fun to try to not get tripped up!
                </p>
                 <p>
                    This project was an exercise in CAD modeling and game design
                    that I took up over the summer between semesters of my grad
                    program.
                </p>

            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="divider"></div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">
            Technical Specs
        </h2>
        <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row ">
            <div class="mx-auto">
                <h3 class="md:text-lg underline">Electronics</h3>
                <ul class="list-disc">
                    <li>ATtiny84</li>
                    <li>TinyTFT</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="divider divider-vertical md:divider-horizontal"></div>
            <div class="mx-auto">
                <h3 class="md:text-lg underline">Fabrication</h3>
                <ul class="list-disc">
                    <li>Autodesk Fusion</li>
                    <li>3D Printing</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <Footer />
</body>

</html>